WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't believe
it's already the end

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.770
of the third season of the show.
-I know. I know.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.637 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I can't keep up anymore.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's crazy.
-It's -- It's flying by.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.273 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It's going so fast.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And -- And one of the things
that is a -- a change is

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like Randall and Beth
were laid out

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.313
as this sort of perfect couple
over the first couple seasons,

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
and -- and this season,
we sort of explore that --

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.584 line:92%
that maybe that's not the case.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Has it been --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.222 size:88% position:44%
Has it been -- I mean,
it's weird to say, like,

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.357 size:84% position:42%
is it fun, as an actor,
to take on that change?

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, of course,
it's a more, you know,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
negative energy to be playing.
-Right.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But do you enjoy it?
-Yeah, negative is always fun

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's, like,
it's challenging.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:32.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Right?

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:35.502
And then, it's a total change-up
from what we have been.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.271 size:84% position:42%
But I kind of feel like
it's realistic, right?

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:38.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's life.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think,
if they stay too perfect,

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
people would start
to question that,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
or people would say, like,
you know,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's not a representation
of a real marriage,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we want to do our best
to really represent

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:48.515 size:84% position:42% line:92%
what people go through.

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.717
So, I found this struggle
to be really challenging,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, you know, I'm doing it
with Sterling K. Brown.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:53.953 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That's not bad with him.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's not
that challenging. Yeah.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You know, it's...

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One thing you had to do
without Sterling

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:01.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
is your character had to rely
on your background.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a dance background,
to some degree.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.231
-'Cause there was
some dancing for you this year.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:05.899 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-There was some dancing.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.767
-Did you have to go back to
the -- to the drawing board?

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you have to retrain at all
for this?

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
They wanted me to do ballet,

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.709
and, like, I left ballet behind,
like, maybe when I was like 14.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Because I didn't like it,

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good reason. Yeah.
-Yeah, that was my thing.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:25.718
I mean, Misty Copeland kills it,
but, like, I --

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.655
but, then,
I went back to train for ballet,

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:31.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I found out
I still didn't like it.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:35.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so, I was like, "Okay.
What we gonna do now?"

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:38.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause they wanna do ballet,
and I was thinking...

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:38.798 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So I asked them.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said,
"Maybe modern dance, y'all.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.234 line:92%
Does she do African dance?

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I can get down with that."

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were like,
"No, it has to be ballet."

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.338 line:92%
So I was like, "All right."

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I got this
brilliant choreographer,

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:51.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nia Brantly, who started
teaching me and coaching me,

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.412 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and she's fantastic.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she made it feel like
it fit my body,

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.616
'cause I'd always sort of
been told, like, you know,

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.618
"Your stomach sticks out,
and your butt's too big" --

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.352 size:78% position:39% line:92%
all these things that

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't kind of fit
into that genre of dance,

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then she made it feel like
I could wear it on my body

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:06.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
and -- and do it
sort of boldly and proudly.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it worked out.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.561
-I feel like, you know...
-It really did work out.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:09.796 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, it worked out.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.798
-I'm glad you -- you guys
put the work in together.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.066
-Yeah. We put a lot of work in.
Yes.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:17.770
-You -- this show, obviously --
I don't need to tell you --

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
has -- the fans
are very passionate about it.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-You --

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are your family members --
are they --

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:25.145
would you would you put them in
the category of passionate fans?

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckling ] Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:30.350
-Oh. Is it good or bad?
-No, it's -- it's -- it's good.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Um, no.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have, like,
this whole text chain.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
My family in Jamaica's
gonna love this

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're --
they're on this text chain,

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:39.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so every time the text,
you know, comes out,

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have commentary
about the show.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:42.795 line:92%
And so, you get different things

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.697
'cause, you know,
people are kind of divided with,

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, there's
a lot going about --

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.234
about Team Beth or Team Randall,
and, you know, so...

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Some people in you family
are not Team Beth?

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Wow.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:53.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, my...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.242
...my family keeps it 150, okay?
It's not...

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So -- So, you know, sometimes,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:02.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, they'll say --
you know -- you know,

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Randall too spoiled.
Him too spoiled.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
You spoil him too much."
You know what I mean?

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, or --
or my niece will say,

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.291
"Um, Auntie Sue, can you
explain to me what your --

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
how you feel about the
Team Randall/Team Beth thing?

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I'm very Team Randall,
and I was wondering

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
what your point of view
would be,

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:20.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
just as a normal person
and not an actress,

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:20.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what..."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.069
"If you were just looking at it
objectively, like,

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
who would you..."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like --
I went to back to --

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"So, you're team who?"

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:28.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like, "Randall."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- But I get it.
I think it's fun.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I mean...

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.346
-And that is a better option
than them not watching the show.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At all.
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I mean --
that means they're tuning in,

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm -- I'm definitely
Team, you know, R&amp;B

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.153
and, you know, hope for the best
for the -- for the couple.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolutely.
-There you go.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, yeah.
-And this is very exciting.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
You shot -- is it
"Won't You Be My Neighbor?"

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:45.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the Tom Hanks film?

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is called now "A Beautiful
Day in the Neighborhood."

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"A Beautiful Day
in the Neighborhood."

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:51.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is the
"Mister Rogers" movie?

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
-Shot in Pittsburgh? Yes?

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:54.734 line:92%
-Shot fully in Pittsburgh

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
except we did a couple days
in New York.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:56.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, cool.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.638
-And was that -- that must have
been a fantastic experience.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was amazing
because I was sandwiched

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:04.844
between Sir Tom Hanks and
Chris Cooper and Matthew Reese,

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so I couldn't ask
for a better cast

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
for my first feature film.
Yeah.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's exciting.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We can't wait to see that.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.318 size:75% position:38%
-And congratulations
on another season.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for
Susan Kelechi Watson,

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

